              <p>Our WordPress website design company invests a lot of effort in creating ADA-compliant digital environments for our clients and their audience. There are four general types of disabilities: visual, hearing, motor, and cognitive. By keeping them all in mind during the <a href="/website-creation-process">website creation process</a>, Alpha Efficiency's talented WordPress designers will ensure that your website is perceivable, operable, understandable, and robust. We focus on all the vital elements for improved accessibility:</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card-list-cards">
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Keyboard navigation</strong><br>If you don't implement clear keyboard navigation on your website, people with motor and visual disabilities will have a hard time exploring it. Alpha Efficiency's WordPress designers and developers are dedicated to implementing all the features necessary for easy website navigation. Your visitors will always know where they are on the website and how to get wherever they want to be without any obstacles.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Form and table labels</strong><br>By utilizing the power of labels, our WordPress designers and developers can make your forms and tables accessible to everyone. They will ensure the forms are easy to use with both keyboard and a mouse and that instructions for filling forms are understandable and helpful.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>CTA buttons</strong><br>Call To Action buttons are a vital element for increasing conversion rates on your website. They help your visitors know what to do next. If you fail to create CTA buttons that give users clear instructions, you might lose many potential customers. Whether you need a fashion eCommerce site, <a href="/web-design-for-plastic-surgery">plastic surgery web design services</a> or a website for any other type of business, our WordPress developers and WordPress designers will ensure that everyone can clearly understand your CTAs.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Colors</strong><br>Using color as the only mean of communication is the wrong approach if you want your website to be ADA-compliant. Our WordPress designers and developers use additional elements, such as patterns, fill, sizing, borders, web design icons, and more, to help you spread messages to people with color blindness. We ensure that the contrast between colors is sufficient enough for everyone to differentiate them.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
                <p><strong>Fonts</strong><br>Fonts are of vital importance for text readability. By choosing suitable font styles and sizes, WordPress website designers from our agency make content readable for everyone. Also, keeping the number of different fonts low and avoiding ones with decorative markings will help you make the website more accessible.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card-list-card">
